@tradition twelve-weeks-aboard
// Twelve weeks aboard (0.92.6 item 7 (c), FX17; lead 35's yes): Day 84 after you came aboard, a Sunday. A toast at the
// Sunday table in the mess hall: Calder says a few words before dinner. Behind P926_TRADS (section 13's P926_NEW).
// STAND-IN WORDS: SW1 writes them (CS1 checks).
k: 711
title: Twelve weeks aboard
when: arrival +84
at: 17:30-17:55
min: 15
prio: 1
where: 3 room Mess hall: mess-seat
hold: 1
who: calder always, torres-zeke always, works 60%, friends-of-host 40%, everyone 15%
anim: talk
host: calder
from: calder

== mail
- Twelve weeks aboard tomorrow. A quick toast in the mess at {time}, before the Sunday table. Don't be late. I'm counting.

== ask
- Twelve weeks! A toast in the mess before dinner.

== here
- To twelve weeks. And the next twelve.   #warm

== thanks
- Calder raises a cup in the mess hall. "Twelve weeks. Still here, still learning. Good." The table drinks to you.   #warm

== chatter
- The new hand's twelve weeks aboard. The Chief made a toast. A short one.   #funny
